dislike BJP': Shehzad Poonawalla on quitting politics; calls rift with brother ideological]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-dislike-bjp-shehzad-poonawalla-on-quitting-politics-calls-rift-with-brother-ideological/articleshow/136058361.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136058361.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Shehzad Poonawalla clarified that his exit from active politics is not due to dislike for the BJP. He expressed his ongoing support for Prime Minister Narendra Modi and other BJP leaders. Differences with his brother Tehseen Poonawalla were framed as a clash of principles rather than personal issues. Shehzad emphasized that every person in India should identify as Hindu.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-dislike-bjp-shehzad-poonawalla-on-quitting-politics-calls-rift-with-brother-ideological/articleshow/136058361.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-dislike-bjp-shehzad-poonawalla-on-quitting-politics-calls-rift-with-brother-ideological/articleshow/136058361.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T21:28:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136058530,imgsize-65448.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nepal PM Balendra Shah to reach Delhi on Sunday for his first foreign bilateral trip - what's on agenda]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nepal-pm-balendra-shah-to-reach-delhi-on-sunday-for-his-first-foreign-bilateral-trip-whats-on-agenda/articleshow/136057927.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136057927.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[htt